{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recorder-events-021-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/SplitEventDetectionTests.cs","line":410,"method":"TreeCreation_BackgroundMap_PopulatedCorrectly","category":"T1","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/RecordingTree.cs:376; any change to RebuildBackgroundMap -> stays green. The test populates tree.BackgroundMap by hand at SplitEventDetectionTests.cs:435 and asserts that same entry back.","what_it_asserts":"That a dictionary entry the test itself wrote is readable, plus indirectly that BuildSplitBranchData gave the background child pid 200.","why_weak":"The comment says it simulates what CreateSplitBranch does, and that is exactly the problem: no production background-map code runs, so a regression in the real population path leaves it green. The sibling TreeCreation_RebuildBackgroundMap_MatchesManualSetup already covers the production path.","proposed_action":"Delete it, or rewrite it to call tree.RebuildBackgroundMap() after adding the two children so the assertions read a production-populated map.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recorder-events-021-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/SplitEventDetectionTests.cs","line":151,"method":"GetEvaBackgroundInitialEnvironmentOverride_UsesBackgroundEvaSpeed","category":"T2","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/ParsekFlight.cs:4991; flip the backgroundSrfSpeed > 0.1 comparison -> red, exactly as it reds the twin cell at SplitEventDetectionTests.cs:127.","what_it_asserts":"That an EVA split from a LANDED vessel with background surface speed 0.0 yields SurfaceStationary.","why_weak":"Identical arguments and identical assertion to GetEvaBackgroundInitialEnvironmentOverride_LandedStationaryShip_ReturnsSurfaceStationary, so it adds no branch coverage; and 0.0 cannot demonstrate which speed source the override reads.","proposed_action":"Delete it, or turn it into the boundary pair the name implies (speed 0.1 -> SurfaceStationary, speed 0.11 -> SurfaceMobile) so the 0.1 threshold itself is pinned.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recorder-events-021-03","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/SplitEventDetectionTests.cs","line":494,"method":"FlightRecorder_JointBreakCheck_DefaultFalse","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/FlightRecorder.cs:276; add an = true initializer to the HasPendingJointBreakCheck auto-property -> red. Nothing else in the class runs during this test.","what_it_asserts":"That a freshly constructed FlightRecorder has HasPendingJointBreakCheck false.","why_weak":"It pins the C# default of an auto-property, not the joint-break signalling contract. The transitions that matter (signal sets it, consume clears it and returns the prior value) have no cell here.","proposed_action":"Keep the default assertion but extend the cell, or add the state-transition cell in the coverage row below.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"FlightRecorder","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/FlightRecorder.cs","sut_line":297,"case_kind":"state-transition","proposed_name":"FlightRecorder_JointBreakSignal_SetsPendingThenConsumeClearsIt","sketch":"Construct a FlightRecorder, assert HasPendingJointBreakCheck is false, invoke the joint-break signal path with a UT, assert the flag is true and PendingJointBreakUT is that UT, then call the consume helper and assert it returned true and the flag is now false and a second consume returns false.","guards":"Catches a regression where the signal never arms or the consume never clears, which would drop or repeat an undock/joint-break branch.","risk":"recording"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"ParsekFlight","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/ParsekFlight.cs","sut_line":4991,"case_kind":"boundary","proposed_name":"GetEvaBackgroundInitialEnvironmentOverride_SpeedAtThreshold_StaysStationary","sketch":"Call GetEvaBackgroundInitialEnvironmentOverride(EVA, true, LANDED, 0.1) and expect SurfaceStationary, then with 0.11 and expect SurfaceMobile; add the SPLASHED and PRELAUNCH situations alongside LANDED.","guards":"Pins the 0.1 m/s threshold and the three surface situations the override accepts; today only LANDED is covered and the threshold value is unpinned.","risk":"recording"}
